## ER Diagram (Text)

```
 ┌────────────┐        ┌──────────────┐
 │    User    │ 1    1 │    Doctor    │
 │------------│◄──────►│--------------│
 │ _id        │(optional)│ _id         │
 │ name       │link      │ name        │
 │ email      │          │ specialization│
 │ password   │          │ email/phone │
 │ role       │          │ availability│
 └─────┬──────┘          └──────┬───────┘
       │ 1                      │ 1
       │ registers               │ is assigned to
       │ *                       │ *
 ┌─────▼──────┐          ┌───────▼────────┐
 │  Patient   │ 1      * │  Appointment   │
 │------------│◄────────►│----------------│
 │ _id        │           │ _id            │
 │ name/age   │           │ patient (FK)   │
 │ gender     │           │ doctor  (FK)   │
 │ medicalHist│           │ date/time      │
 └─────┬──────┘           │ status         │
       │ 1                └───────┬────────┘
       │ has                      │ 0..1
       │ *                        │ generates
 ┌─────▼──────┐                   │
 │    Bill    │◄──────────────────┘
 │------------│
 │ _id        │
 │ patient(FK)│
 │ appointment(FK, optional)│
 │ treatments[]│
 │ totalAmount │
 │ paymentStatus│
 └────────────┘
```

**Relationships:**
- One `User` (role=doctor) can optionally link to one `Doctor` profile (1:1).
- One `Doctor` has many `Appointment`s (1:N).
- One `Patient` has many `Appointment`s and many `Bill`s (1:N each).
- One `Appointment` can generate at most one `Bill` (1:0..1).
- `User` (admin/receptionist) creates/registers many `Patient`s, `Appointment`s, and `Bill`s (audit trail via `createdBy` / `registeredBy` / `generatedBy`).

